<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $21.8 mln Feb 24.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $21.8 mln Feb 24.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $21.8 million deficit on Feb 24 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON FEBRUARY 24</p>
<p>Exports: $181.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $196 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $187.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $194.2 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $21.8 million</p>
<p>FEBRUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.552 million</p>
<p>Imports: $2.500 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.774 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.701 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.125 billion ((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248-5418))</p>
</text>
